From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:55:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] workspace: don't wait for non-desktop outputs to turn off

maybeUpdateDpmsState() went to Off, and released the "turning screens
off" sleep inhibitor, only once every backend output reported DpmsMode
Off. applyOutputChanges() leaves non-desktop outputs alone (they are for
leasing: VR headsets, a phone's cover display), so their dpms mode never
changes, Off is never reached, and logind waits InhibitDelayMaxSec (5 s)
on every suspend with the lock screen up. On a Galaxy Z Flip3, whose
cover display is leased to a client, that was every one of 125 suspends
in a day.

Skip non-desktop outputs there, and when deciding that there is no
output to turn off at all. The virtual backend gains non-desktop outputs
for the test, left alone by applyChanges() as the DRM backend does.
